From f432fb83f6d84612cf53138ff6cda07a382f3d0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicole@muzz.in>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:28:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] grid: clamp a definite preferred size by min/max size in
 minimum contributions

When an item has a definite preferred size its minimum contribution is its
min-content contribution, and that contribution is the preferred size
clamped by the item's min and max sizes. minimum_contribution() returned
the raw preferred size instead, so an item with width:1120px and
max-width:1008px placed in a 1fr column grew the column to 1120px and the
grid overflowed its container (reddit scrolled sideways because of this).

https://www.w3.org/TR/css-grid-2/#min-size-auto

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/compute/grid/types/grid_item.rs           | 23 ++++++++++++------
 ...em_preferred_size_clamped_by_max_size.html | 18 ++++++++++++++
 ...ze_clamped_by_max_size__border_box_ltr.xml | 15 ++++++++++++
 ...ze_clamped_by_max_size__border_box_rtl.xml | 15 ++++++++++++
